WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.291
Punctuation Traps: When NOT to Punctuate

00:00:03.671 --> 00:00:06.050
No rule? No punctuation.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:08.341
How to spot it

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.857
One choice with no punctuation

00:00:11.407 --> 00:00:13.521
A long subject before the verb

00:00:14.071 --> 00:00:17.999
It’s testing: resisting punctuation that isn’t needed

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:19.965
The method

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:22.761
Step 1: Name the parts

00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:24.775
Subject, verb, object?

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.134
Step 2: Do they belong together?

00:00:28.414 --> 00:00:31.521
Subject–verb, verb–object: no mark.

00:00:32.071 --> 00:00:34.188
Step 3: Name the rule

00:00:34.468 --> 00:00:36.778
Can’t name one? Cut the mark.

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:38.423
In a few words

00:00:38.573 --> 00:00:40.952
No rule? No punctuation.

00:00:42.152 --> 00:00:42.934
The rules

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.586
Nothing between subject and verb

00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:48.755
Wrong: The results of the study, showed…

00:00:49.035 --> 00:00:51.764
Right: The results of the study showed…

00:00:52.314 --> 00:00:53.893
Nothing before “that”

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:56.049
Wrong: Researchers found, that…

00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:58.411
Right: Researchers found that…

00:00:58.961 --> 00:01:00.679
Nothing after “such as”

00:01:00.959 --> 00:01:03.296
Wrong: such as: oak and maple

00:01:03.576 --> 00:01:05.975
Right: such as oak and maple

00:01:06.525 --> 00:01:08.700
Lists of three: commas between

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.896
Right: ropes, tents, and food

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:13.703
Blended quotes: no comma

00:01:13.983 --> 00:01:16.307
Wrong: called it, “a triumph”

00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:18.412
Right: called it “a triumph”

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.673
Let’s try one

00:01:21.073 --> 00:01:26.630
The researchers who spent three winters tracking the migration of snow geese across the Canadian

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.825
Arctic ______ that the birds’ routes had shifted east.

00:01:30.475 --> 00:01:32.728
This whole chunk is one long subject.

00:01:33.278 --> 00:01:38.459
Then the verb, concluded, then what they concluded. These parts belong together.

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:42.010
So no punctuation anywhere. Choice A.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.279
Common traps

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:45.767
The breath comma

00:01:46.047 --> 00:01:49.248
A long subject makes you want to pause. Don’t.

00:01:49.798 --> 00:01:51.444
Colon after “including”

00:01:51.724 --> 00:01:52.314
Never.

00:01:53.514 --> 00:01:56.205
Punctuation Traps: When NOT to Punctuate

00:01:56.485 --> 00:01:58.865
No rule? No punctuation.

00:01:59.415 --> 00:01:59.994
Spot it

00:02:00.194 --> 00:02:03.834
One choice has no punctuation; long subject

00:02:04.384 --> 00:02:05.091
Steps

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.587
1. Name the parts: subject, verb, object

00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:11.538
2. Belong together? → no mark

00:02:11.818 --> 00:02:14.864
3. Can’t name a rule? → cut the mark

00:02:15.414 --> 00:02:16.139
Remember

00:02:16.339 --> 00:02:18.591
Nothing between subject and verb

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.449
Nothing before “that”

00:02:20.729 --> 00:02:23.218
Nothing after “such as” / “including”

00:02:23.498 --> 00:02:25.715
Blended quote: no comma

00:02:26.265 --> 00:02:26.705
Trap

00:02:26.905 --> 00:02:29.384
The breath comma after a long subject

